1
00:00:00,375 --> 00:00:01,708
Let's do Cake at Stake!

2
00:00:01,708 --> 00:00:05,625
I really do not like Cake at Stake!

3
00:00:05,750 --> 00:00:09,708
Oh, do you not? I guess we'll take the shortcut and
eliminate you immediately, then.

4
00:00:09,750 --> 00:00:12,916
I really like Cake at Stake.

5
00:00:12,958 --> 00:00:13,541
That's better!

6
00:00:13,750 --> 00:00:15,041
Now we can do Cake at Stake!

7
00:00:15,125 --> 00:00:15,916
♪ Da-da-da-da-da-da ♪

8
00:00:15,916 --> 00:00:17,375
♪ Cake at Stake! ♪

9
00:00:17,541 --> 00:00:19,625
So, the team who lost will do Cake at Stake.

10
00:00:20,166 --> 00:00:22,916
If you remember from last time, good ol' SB ripped the tie.

11
00:00:22,916 --> 00:00:24,583
So, the Grapes won the tiebreaker.

12
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:25,583
Announcer:
The Cherries lost.

13
00:00:26,041 --> 00:00:27,093
Hee-lo, Cherries!

14
00:00:27,416 --> 00:00:28,666
So, you know the rules:

15
00:00:28,666 --> 00:00:31,083
The one Cherry who doesn't receive cake goes home.

16
00:00:31,458 --> 00:00:33,458
I mean, the TLC if you remember.

17
00:00:33,791 --> 00:00:35,750
Cherries, this is your fourth time here.

18
00:00:36,208 --> 00:00:37,041
Getting used to it?

19
00:00:37,041 --> 00:00:38,541
Just get on with it!

20
00:00:38,541 --> 00:00:41,666
The cake was too expensive, so I got six cupcakes instead.

21
00:00:41,958 --> 00:00:43,791
But think, there are only six.

22
00:00:44,083 --> 00:00:47,625
Anyway, we got thirteen votes.
That's one fewer than last time.

23
00:00:47,791 --> 00:00:49,541
It's the first time it's ever gone down.

24
00:00:49,791 --> 00:00:54,000
[SLOWED DOWN]
I want to cry now. I really do.

25
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:56,416
Yeah, I don't, like, think so.

26
00:00:56,541 --> 00:00:58,250
ANNOUNCER:
Pin, you have two win tokens.

27
00:00:58,375 --> 00:00:59,625
Would you like to use one now?

28
00:00:59,791 --> 00:01:00,708
Uh, no.

29
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:02,500
I mean, there's nothing mean I-

30
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:03,583
Yeah, yeah. We know.

31
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:05,625
Oh, I just knew you were gonna say that.

32
00:01:05,791 --> 00:01:06,875
'Cause I'm just so smart!

33
00:01:06,958 --> 00:01:07,875
Yeah, not really.

34
00:01:08,291 --> 00:01:10,333
On the test, you scored fourteen out of twenty.

35
00:01:10,458 --> 00:01:12,375
Or seventy percent, which is a C minus.

36
00:01:12,375 --> 00:01:14,375
ERASER:
Ooooh! Burn!

37
00:01:14,375 --> 00:01:16,083
So, here are the seven cherries.

38
00:01:16,375 --> 00:01:17,583
And here are the thirteen votes.

39
00:01:18,041 --> 00:01:19,708
Only one of you got zero votes.

40
00:01:20,166 --> 00:01:20,750
Firey...

41
00:01:20,750 --> 00:01:23,208
Thank you! I needed to hear that!

42
00:01:23,208 --> 00:01:25,166
You are not the person who got zero votes.

43
00:01:25,208 --> 00:01:26,791
Oh my gosh! No fair!

44
00:01:26,958 --> 00:01:28,291
- ANNOUNCER: It's Pencil.
- PENCIL: Yoy!

45
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:31,958
ANNOUNCER:
Bubble, Firey, and Match; you all got one vote each.

46
00:01:31,958 --> 00:01:32,291
[THROWS CAKES OFF-SCREEN]

47
00:01:32,291 --> 00:01:33,083
ANNOUNCER:
Happy, Match?

48
00:01:33,208 --> 00:01:35,166
I didn't even say the word "a piece."

49
00:01:35,166 --> 00:01:38,583
Ugh! He said it! I'm so, like, not happy!

50
00:01:38,958 --> 00:01:40,500
Cherries, I'll tell you this:

51
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:42,916
ANNOUNCER:
None of the remaining three of you
got the same number of votes.

52
00:01:43,208 --> 00:01:44,666
Eraser, look!

53
00:01:44,666 --> 00:01:50,208
Pin has to get out! If she doesn't,
one of us is going to the TLC!

54
00:01:50,208 --> 00:01:54,583
You remember how devastating it was
when it was Blocky's time to go!

55
00:01:54,583 --> 00:01:55,833
It can't happen again!

56
00:01:55,833 --> 00:01:57,666
Eraser, the number of votes you got is the

57
00:01:57,666 --> 00:02:00,041
factorial of the difference of the square of the number of
spacial dimensions in this universe,

58
00:02:00,041 --> 00:02:01,375
and one more than the smallest perfect number.

59
00:02:01,416 --> 00:02:03,250
ERASER:
And that is?

60
00:02:03,250 --> 00:02:04,958
Nine. You are eliminated.

61
00:02:05,333 --> 00:02:06,041
Ha ha!

62
00:02:06,041 --> 00:02:08,458
If you were smart, you'd know the result is actually two.

63
00:02:08,458 --> 00:02:10,166
I guess you are not so smart after all!

64
00:02:10,166 --> 00:02:11,625
Grrrr!

65
00:02:12,291 --> 00:02:15,041
Pin, Pen, you are the final two.

66
00:02:15,375 --> 00:02:17,791
And your names sound alike. That's cool.

67
00:02:18,208 --> 00:02:20,250
Cool as Ice Cube because she's frozen!

68
00:02:20,666 --> 00:02:23,708
But Ice Cube, what are you doing here?
You're on the other team!

69
00:02:23,833 --> 00:02:25,291
Ahhhhh!

70
00:02:25,291 --> 00:02:26,583
I have the last cupcake.

71
00:02:26,958 --> 00:02:28,291
Is it for Pen, or for Pin?

72
00:02:28,416 --> 00:02:30,166
Uhm, Mister Speaker Thing?

73
00:02:30,708 --> 00:02:33,250
MATCH:
I see Pen's name written on the cupcake!

74
00:02:33,583 --> 00:02:36,583
Hey! I see mine on mine, too!

75
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:38,166
[EVERYONE AGREES]

76
00:02:38,458 --> 00:02:42,416
So, does that mean the cupcake's mine and I'm safe?

77
00:02:42,416 --> 00:02:43,541
ANNOUNCER:
Uh, yeah, it does.

78
00:02:43,916 --> 00:02:45,750
That name was not supposed to be there.

79
00:02:46,208 --> 00:02:47,500
So, goodbye, Pin.

80
00:02:47,708 --> 00:02:48,958
I use my win token!

81
00:02:48,958 --> 00:02:49,583
ANNOUNCER:
Too late!

82
00:02:49,583 --> 00:02:51,666
But I'm the team leader! You can't do that!

83
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:52,500
Oh no!

84
00:02:52,833 --> 00:02:55,291
Eraser, you need a heroic leader like me!

85
00:02:58,416 --> 00:03:01,625
That Pin got what she deserved!

86
00:03:02,125 --> 00:03:05,000
Let that be a lesson:
Use your win tokens before it's too late.

87
00:03:05,208 --> 00:03:11,833
[INTRO PLAYS]

88
00:03:11,833 --> 00:03:14,291
Subtitles: TAFFYMARZI

89
00:03:14,291 --> 00:03:15,083
Look at this!

90
00:03:19,125 --> 00:03:23,541
But in this next contest, teams temporarily
will temporarily be temporarily formed temporarily-

91
00:03:23,541 --> 00:03:24,583
within the teams...

92
00:03:24,583 --> 00:03:25,333
TEMPORARILY.

93
00:03:25,416 --> 00:03:27,541
That's why it's teams in teams!

94
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,750
The Cherries will become two teams of three,
and the Grapes will be three teams of three.

95
00:03:32,208 --> 00:03:32,750
Got that?

96
00:03:32,875 --> 00:03:34,250
Yeah, I guess?

97
00:03:34,250 --> 00:03:36,416
ANNOUNCER:
Our TV will randomly choose teams.

98
00:03:37,208 --> 00:03:39,333
ANNOUNCER:
So, Bubble, here's who you will be teamed with.

99
00:03:39,541 --> 00:03:43,250
OM Geez, people! I hope our alliance will be
together as a team!

100
00:03:43,250 --> 00:03:44,250
- Match...
- Yeah!

101
00:03:44,250 --> 00:03:44,833
ANNOUNCER:
And the other one is-

102
00:03:44,833 --> 00:03:47,250
It's, like, so gotta be me!

103
00:03:47,333 --> 00:03:47,833
ANNOUNCER:
Pencil.

104
00:03:48,250 --> 00:03:50,375
Yes! This is, like, a miracle!

105
00:03:50,375 --> 00:03:52,708
So, the remaining Cherries form another team.

106
00:03:53,041 --> 00:03:53,708
ANNOUNCER:
Grape time.

107
00:03:53,708 --> 00:03:54,791
ANNOUNCER:
There are nine of you.

108
00:03:54,791 --> 00:03:56,250
ANNOUNCER:
Snowball is grouped with Rocky.

109
00:03:56,250 --> 00:04:01,458
Oh, great! That's helpful!
He doesn't even have arms!

110
00:04:01,458 --> 00:04:02,458
ANNOUNCER:
And Golf Ball.

111
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:06,000
NOOOOOOO!

112
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,291
- ANNOUNCER: Don't they make a great team?
- NOOOOOOO!

113
00:04:07,291 --> 00:04:17,083
NOOOOOOO!

114
00:04:17,875 --> 00:04:20,375
ANNOUNCER:
The other teams are Leafy, Tennis Ball, and Teardrop.

115
00:04:20,708 --> 00:04:22,541
ANNOUNCER:
And Coiny, Ice Cube, and Needle.

116
00:04:22,791 --> 00:04:24,750
So what will you five teams be doing?

117
00:04:25,291 --> 00:04:26,424
It will be three islands.

118
00:04:26,875 --> 00:04:28,583
You will go through all of them in sequence.

119
00:04:28,583 --> 00:04:30,958
Is one of them Dream Island?

120
00:04:31,166 --> 00:04:34,083
Because that would be something I'd really like to-

121
00:04:34,083 --> 00:04:36,041
No. None of the islands are Dream Island.

122
00:04:44,458 --> 00:04:45,625
So, yeah, to start:

123
00:04:45,625 --> 00:04:47,791
Cross that balance beam to get to Island 1.

124
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:52,250
PENCIL:
We're in first! We're so going to win this!

125
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,250
Look! You weaklings better not make me lose here!

126
00:04:57,250 --> 00:04:59,125
What? You're the only one who matters?

127
00:04:59,125 --> 00:05:00,833
Yeah, duh I am!

128
00:05:01,083 --> 00:05:02,791
Wow, you're stupid.

129
00:05:02,791 --> 00:05:04,708
Woah! I'm the stupid one?!

130
00:05:04,708 --> 00:05:05,875
SNOWBALL:
Yeah you are!

131
00:05:06,166 --> 00:05:09,750
'Cause anyone normal would actually start the race!

132
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:11,666
Which is what I'm doing!

133
00:05:11,833 --> 00:05:13,208
Come on, Rocky!

134
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:15,750
Yeah! Let's do this, TD!

135
00:05:15,750 --> 00:05:17,250
Slow and steady!

136
00:05:17,708 --> 00:05:19,041
Out of my way!

137
00:05:19,708 --> 00:05:20,291
Bleh!

138
00:05:28,875 --> 00:05:32,041
Ice Cube! Ice Cube! Where are you?!

139
00:05:32,791 --> 00:05:36,416
Hmm, I'll just get to Island 1 and wait for her there.

140
00:05:37,083 --> 00:05:40,708
That SB is a rager! I hate him!

141
00:05:40,708 --> 00:05:42,583
So, what do we do now?

142
00:05:42,750 --> 00:05:48,125
We'll have to swim to Island 1!
There's no way we could get back on!

143
00:05:50,125 --> 00:05:51,041
Woooah!

144
00:05:51,041 --> 00:05:52,041
Go get GB.

145
00:05:52,041 --> 00:05:55,375
Well, I'll have to plow through all those people!

146
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:56,041
ANNOUNCER:
No plowing.

147
00:05:56,250 --> 00:05:56,833
Swim back.

148
00:05:57,041 --> 00:05:58,458
If you don't, I'll eliminate you.

149
00:05:58,458 --> 00:06:00,875
SNOWBALL:
Why do I have to do this?!

150
00:06:00,875 --> 00:06:03,125
A team has to stick together. Now go.

151
00:06:03,125 --> 00:06:04,916
SNOWBALL:
Ugh, fine!

152
00:06:08,666 --> 00:06:10,958
Why is he swimming back?

153
00:06:11,166 --> 00:06:12,166
Dunno!

154
00:06:13,041 --> 00:06:15,833
Yeah! I think we're the first team here!

155
00:06:16,375 --> 00:06:17,000
LEAFY:
Woah.

156
00:06:24,666 --> 00:06:27,083
Okay, let's get started!
Push!

157
00:06:29,875 --> 00:06:32,530
Seven, four, nine...

158
00:06:33,041 --> 00:06:33,750
Ugh!

159
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:35,291
It's a teddy bear.

160
00:06:36,583 --> 00:06:40,375
Where's Ice Cube?
Do you know where she is, Needy?

161
00:06:40,708 --> 00:06:43,041
Don't call me Needy! But, no.

162
00:06:46,333 --> 00:06:50,708
Hey, we're still in second!
We didn't fall too hard behind!

163
00:06:51,333 --> 00:06:53,916
Gosh, GB! I'm here!

164
00:06:57,250 --> 00:07:00,416
Ice Cube! I've been wondering where you were!

165
00:07:01,458 --> 00:07:02,460
Woaaah!

166
00:07:03,083 --> 00:07:07,916
Eraser? Isn't water Firey's poison? He'll die!

167
00:07:07,916 --> 00:07:12,625
ERASER:
Oh! Oh yeah, we'll have to go back and turn on the FRC.

168
00:07:13,250 --> 00:07:15,208
What? A baseball bat?!

169
00:07:16,041 --> 00:07:18,375
Three, six, three!

170
00:07:19,708 --> 00:07:22,791
An egg? What good's an egg?!

171
00:07:23,333 --> 00:07:27,083
Ice Cube, because of what just happened,
I think we need a team leader!

172
00:07:27,083 --> 00:07:28,166
- Can I be-
- NO!

173
00:07:28,166 --> 00:07:29,666
I'll be the team leader!

174
00:07:29,666 --> 00:07:31,666
We must be in last now.

175
00:07:31,916 --> 00:07:34,333
What? It has to warm up?

176
00:07:34,791 --> 00:07:35,958
A flower.

177
00:07:35,958 --> 00:07:38,000
Oh, I don't like Flower. She's mean.

178
00:07:38,500 --> 00:07:39,000
Aww!

179
00:07:39,458 --> 00:07:43,083
Hey, hey! Pretty simple, but that's the raft!

180
00:07:43,083 --> 00:07:45,083
Great, we've got a lead!

181
00:07:45,375 --> 00:07:47,666
Come on guys! I'm here!

182
00:07:47,875 --> 00:07:50,000
Sixty percent done warming up!

183
00:07:51,625 --> 00:07:52,625
Okay, we got it!

184
00:07:52,625 --> 00:07:54,208
TENNIS BALL:
We fell to third!

185
00:07:54,375 --> 00:07:55,403
Is it it? Is it it?

186
00:07:55,403 --> 00:07:56,000
Ugh!

187
00:08:02,208 --> 00:08:03,625
Build! Let's build!

188
00:08:05,125 --> 00:08:06,070
Finally!

189
00:08:06,291 --> 00:08:08,791
ERASER:
Come on, Firey! Don't fall this time!

190
00:08:09,291 --> 00:08:10,625
It's not it again!

191
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:13,013
Wait, Match!

192
00:08:17,125 --> 00:08:19,791
Gotcha! Whew, this is great!

193
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:23,500
Snowball! That method of stacking is very unstable-

194
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:24,291
Shut it!

195
00:08:24,666 --> 00:08:25,916
- That's it!
- Yes!

196
00:08:25,916 --> 00:08:26,708
Let's go!

197
00:08:26,875 --> 00:08:29,958
Oh no! We're the only ones still here!

198
00:08:29,958 --> 00:08:32,375
LEAFY:
Yeah, TD! You got this!

199
00:08:32,375 --> 00:08:33,375
Woooah!

200
00:08:34,250 --> 00:08:35,750
What did I tell you?!

201
00:08:35,750 --> 00:08:36,375
SNOWBALL:
Grrr!

202
00:08:36,750 --> 00:08:37,833
Island 3!

203
00:08:47,875 --> 00:08:50,875
No, it doesn't work! We'll have to go back!

204
00:08:52,041 --> 00:08:54,541
FIREY:
Yeah! Got the raft on the first try!

205
00:08:55,041 --> 00:08:56,236
Let's go!

206
00:08:56,458 --> 00:08:58,291
Hey, you forgot about Pencil!

207
00:08:58,291 --> 00:08:59,958
Let's turn around!

208
00:09:02,291 --> 00:09:05,375
Our key is a fake! It won't unlock!

209
00:09:05,541 --> 00:09:07,166
Let's turn around.

210
00:09:07,666 --> 00:09:09,500
I'm so disappointed!

211
00:09:09,625 --> 00:09:11,583
Snowball, you never learn, do you?

212
00:09:11,833 --> 00:09:14,458
Hey, three teams are still here!

213
00:09:14,666 --> 00:09:16,416
We're still in this!

214
00:09:16,625 --> 00:09:19,666
There's no time to be Mr. Nice Guy!

215
00:09:19,666 --> 00:09:20,083
Oof!

216
00:09:20,083 --> 00:09:23,375
GOLF BALL:
SB, next time, build a stable structure!

217
00:09:23,375 --> 00:09:24,958
So, where's Pencil?

218
00:09:24,958 --> 00:09:26,333
She must be in one of the safes!

219
00:09:26,708 --> 00:09:27,750
BUBBLE:
She's not in this one!

220
00:09:27,750 --> 00:09:30,000
Or this one! Or this one! Or this one!

221
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:33,750
If we could just climb the pole, we'd be in first!

222
00:09:33,750 --> 00:09:34,958
I'll try!

223
00:09:35,333 --> 00:09:36,481
Oh my gosh, it's slippery!

224
00:09:36,708 --> 00:09:37,750
Okay, I got it!

225
00:09:38,083 --> 00:09:39,666
Pencil! You're here!

226
00:09:39,666 --> 00:09:41,541
Now let's go super fast!

227
00:09:41,541 --> 00:09:43,875
Huurgh... HuuuyYAH!

228
00:09:45,125 --> 00:09:46,958
I think we're still in first!

229
00:09:47,375 --> 00:09:49,250
It doesn't unlock again!

230
00:09:49,541 --> 00:09:50,250
Gotcha!

231
00:09:50,458 --> 00:09:51,250
Go, go, go!

232
00:09:51,625 --> 00:09:53,708
- Yeah, it works!
- Alright!

233
00:09:54,708 --> 00:09:57,708
Hey, it's the Speaker Thing!

234
00:09:57,708 --> 00:10:01,500
Pen, Eraser, Firey, you're the first team to finish.
You each get a win token. Leave.

235
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:02,875
[EVERYONE SCREAMS]

236
00:10:03,208 --> 00:10:04,315
We're in!

237
00:10:05,250 --> 00:10:06,500
You're team two. Leave.

238
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:07,291
[EVERYONE SCREAMS]

239
00:10:10,291 --> 00:10:11,625
- Got it!
- Got it!
- Got it!

240
00:10:11,625 --> 00:10:13,500
Paddle fast, fast, fast!

241
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:16,791
We wouldn't be behind if you two could paddle!

242
00:10:17,041 --> 00:10:18,041
Here we go!

243
00:10:19,208 --> 00:10:21,000
- Team three.
- Yes!

244
00:10:21,458 --> 00:10:24,000
[EVERYONE SCREAMS]

245
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:25,291
It works!

246
00:10:25,500 --> 00:10:26,833
SNOWBALL:
OUT OF MY WAY!

247
00:10:27,166 --> 00:10:30,166
SB, GB, Rocky, you're team four, so you're all safe. Leave.

248
00:10:30,333 --> 00:10:31,250
[EVERYONE SCREAMS]

249
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:32,125
Coiny, Icy, Needy-

250
00:10:32,125 --> 00:10:34,375
You're in fifth, last team. One of you will be eliminated.

251
00:10:34,375 --> 00:10:37,666
♪ Coiny, Ice Cube, and Needle: No! No! No! No! No! ♪
Announcer: Viewers out there, vote between Coiny,
Ice Cube, and Needle.

252
00:10:37,666 --> 00:10:46,125
♪ Coiny, Ice Cube, and Needle: No! No! No! No! No! ♪

